From 21811369aab6c39f84e83378c6ed3b4470be9ca7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yihou <yihou@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:43:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/25] fix(image): carry the sglang mooncake early-send KV
 wait-event patch

From PR #56 (liyingli), reduced to the part this merge actually exercised.

Without it, mooncake's transfer worker RDMA-reads a non-final prefill chunk's
pages while the forward that writes them is still running. Prompts longer than
one chunk come back partially wrong and nothing raises: on GLM-5.2 DSA a needle
read returns the leading digits and then cycles the closing tag, and the
corruption boundary lands exactly on the chunk boundary. mori/conn.py already
waited on the completion event prefill.py records; mooncake/conn.py had no
wait_event or synchronize() anywhere.

Squashes PR#56's 0360af5 (the hand-cut diff) and 6121189 (its re-cut as a
self-locating script + the Dockerfile wiring) into their end state, since the
intermediate diff was dropped by the second commit anyway.

Deliberately NOT taken from those commits:

  * deploy/docker/Dockerfile.sglang.gfx942 -- the same layer for the MI325X
    image. We never built or ran that image in this merge; PR #56 carries it.

Validated here by G2: a 24k prompt really split into 8192+8192+1728 returns the
needle at all 5 depths, all finish=stop, and conc=128 shows 0 corrupt.

Co-authored-by: liyingli <liyingli@amd.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
